OL,3,GNEWSAResidents celebrate as
OL,4,Aregeneration scheme scrapped
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents who opposed a #2.2bn
OL,7,Fregeneration project have welcomed its
OL,8,Fcollapse, but say the area still needs
OL,9,Finvestment and improvement.
OL,11,FBirmingham City Council announced it
OL,12,Fhad "mutually agreed" to part ways with
OL,13,Fdeveloper Berkeley St Joseph after
OL,14,Frising costs and a challenging economic
OL,15,Fclimate made plans for Ladywood
OL,16,Funviable.
OL,18,FThe proposed development, which would
OL,19,Fhave included thousands of new homes,
OL,20,Fgreen spaces and transport
OL,21,Fimprovements, faced criticism from some
OL,22,Fresidents.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,353,350,200,160,0,100
